<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Swami Vivekananda, 35, comes for his preventive visit three weeks after diabetes was confirmed. He takes metformin extended-release 1000 mg with the evening meal; the loose stools of the first week have settled. His thirst has eased, he gets up to pass urine once a night instead of three times, and his fasting readings on the home meter are 138 to 162 mg/dL. He has seen the dietitian. His home blood pressure averaged 136/86 over seven days. He kept the fortnightly fast last week with fruit, milk and water, as planned, without symptoms. He still lies awake for about two hours before he falls asleep. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic preventive visit, age 35</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Type 2 diabetes, new; moderately increased albuminuria, to be confirmed; raised blood pressure; mixed hyperlipidemia; long-standing insomnia</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Metformin extended-release 1000 mg with the evening meal</td></tr><tr><td>Home readings</td><td>Fasting glucose 138 to 162 mg/dL; blood pressure average 136/86</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper before the visit and reviewed with him by Dr. Thornbury-Mensah. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair, and improving</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives in community with his brother monks and disciples; purposeful work; his faith and practice</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No tobacco use now</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>None, by his vows (AUDIT-C 0)</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks by the river each morning and evening; rides when he can</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Mostly vegetarian monastery meals with fish at some; fewer sweets since seeing the dietitian; fasts twice a month</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Two hours to fall asleep most nights; rises before dawn; five hours&apos; sleep</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes distress</td><td>Low; he regards the illness calmly but wants it understood</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No firearms; no violence</td></tr><tr><td>Travel</td><td>Plans to spend the summer and autumn travelling in the mountains</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

