    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Negative</td><td>Energy better; weight steady at 73 kg after the earlier loss</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Negative</td><td>Reading vision a little blurred when glucose was high, now clearer</td></tr><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Negative</td><td>No mouth or gum problems</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Negative</td><td>No cough or breathlessness</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No chest pain, palpitations or ankle swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>Loose stools of the first week of metformin settled</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Positive</td><td>Gets up once a night to pass urine, down from three times</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No joint pain</td></tr><tr><td>Integumentary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No foot sores or skin infections</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No numbness or tingling in the feet</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Negative</td><td>Mood steady; PHQ-9 3, from sleep and tiredness; GAD-7 2</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>11 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
