    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, anxiety and alcohol screens are negative. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension, stage 1 (I10)</content>. Home average 136/86 confirms stage 1 hypertension. With diabetes and a urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio of 46 mg/g, the target is below 130/80 and an ARB protects the kidneys; an ARB is chosen over an ACE inhibitor so that a cough does not confuse matters. [S]<list><item>Losartan 25 mg daily.</item><item>Potassium and creatinine in two weeks.</item><item>Home readings continue; less salt in cooking.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mixed hyperlipidemia (E78.2)</content>. LDL 132 and triglycerides 228 at 35 with diabetes, South Asian ancestry, albuminuria and hypertension: a moderate-intensity statin is reasonable even before 40. He asked for time to think. [S]<list><item>Decision at the next visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Screening for a man born in India</content>. Hepatitis B and latent tuberculosis screening are recommended for people born where they are common; HIV and hepatitis C once in adulthood. [S]<list><item>Hepatitis B surface antigen, surface antibody and core antibody, interferon-gamma release assay, HIV and hepatitis C antibody drawn today.</item><item>Hepatitis B vaccine series started today; Tdap today.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>134/84 in clinic; home 136/86; treatment started</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 3; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GAD-7 score 2</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Born in a country where hepatitis B is common; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Latent tuberculosis infection screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Born in a country where tuberculosis is common; interferon-gamma release assay drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>HIV and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once-in-adulthood tests drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol</td><td>Up to date</td><td>A1c 9.4 percent and lipids three weeks ago; under treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetic eye examination</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Retinal photographs booked for the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal and prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not due at 35</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap given; no adult record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>HepB-CpG dose 1 of 2 (diabetes, age 19 to 59)</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 three weeks ago (diabetes)</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Given three weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>From 50</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine (no record of a tetanus vaccine in adulthood); Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 10. Cardiovascular Disease and Risk Management: Standards of Care in Diabetes-2026 (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Potassium and creatinine with the diabetes review in two weeks, with retinal photographs and the screening results. Hepatitis B dose 2 in a month or on his return. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1898-03-23: five-week diabetes review before a long journey: glucose log, metformin dose, kidney function and potassium on losartan, repeat urine albumin, retinal photographs, statin, and a travel and fasting plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
