    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent. He named a health care agent, a brother monk of his order, recorded in the confidential part of the chart and not named here. He wants treatment for any illness he could recover from. If he were dying, he would want to be at the monastery, not in a hospital, with the rites of his tradition and with chanting, and without measures that would only prolong dying. He asked that the clinic respect his monastic practices and his fasting at the end of life as at other times. To be revisited at any change in his health and at least yearly. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
